        "name": "Escaping",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The term is percent-encoded with urllib.parse.quote(term, safe=\"\") and the resulting URL is HTML-escaped with html.escape(quote=True) in the href, while the visible text is escaped with html.escape, so payloads like `\"><script>x</script>` or `a&b=c` cannot break out of either context."
      },
      {
        "name": "Behavior",
